     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Bethany Seeger",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "2018-11-08T12:19:25.029-0400"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/362a60c7c1f37ec3362a1f5d4f2b7eb5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBS-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Bethany Seeger",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I don't think it's necessary to have an Accept header in the response to a GET on a timemap.  And there's nothing to say we have to advertise 'application/link-format' -  it's just expected that we support it. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-5"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-5",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "GET /timemap/http://a.example.org/ HTTP/1.1\r\n   Host: arxiv.example.net\r\n   Accept: application/link-format;q=1.0\r\n   Connection: close\r\n\r\n                     Figure 27: Request for a TimeMap\r\n\r\n   If the TimeMap requested by the user agent exists, the server's\r\n   response has a \"200 OK\" HTTP status code and the list of Mementos is\r\n   provided in the entity-body of the response.  Such a response is\r\n   shown in Figure 28.\r\n\r\n   HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n   Date: Thu, 21 Jan 2010 00:06:50 GMT\r\n   Server: Apache\r\n   Content-Length: 4883\r\n   Content-Type: application/link-format\r\n   Connection: close",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "codeBlock"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We could include a Vary field to indicate that \"Accept\" will function on this resource.  That field exists when one requests a timemap w/o an Accept type.  But it doesn't get returned if you sent in an Accept header, like so:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "curl localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -vv -H \"Accept: application/link-format\"\r\n\r\n< HTTP/1.1 200 \r\n< Cache-Control: private\r\n< Expires: Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT\r\n< Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID=E28D3BEA8111021304AD69D52B6E8CD4; Path=/fcrepo5; HttpOnly\r\n< Set-Cookie: rememberMe=deleteMe; Path=/fcrepo5; Max-Age=0; Expires=Wed, 07-Nov-2018 17:11:40 GMT\r\n< Link: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#Resource>;rel=\"type\"\r\n< Link: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#Container>;rel=\"type\"\r\n< Link: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#RDFSource>; rel=\"type\"\r\n< Link: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer>;rel=\"type\"\r\n< Link: <http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog>; rel=\"timegate\"\r\n< Link: <http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog>; rel=\"original\"\r\n< Link: <http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions>; rel=\"timemap\"\r\n< Link: <http://mementoweb.org/ns#TimeMap>; rel=\"type\"\r\n< Accept-External-Content-Handling: copy,redirect,proxy\r\n< Vary-Post: Memento-Datetime\r\n< Accept-Post: text/turtle,text/rdf+n3,text/n3,application/rdf+xml,application/n-triples,application/ld+json\r\n< Allow: POST,HEAD,GET,OPTIONS\r\n< Link: <http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions/fcr:acl>; rel=\"acl\"\r\n< Content-Type: application/link-format\r\n< Content-Length: 236\r\n< Date: Thu, 08 Nov 2018 17:11:40 GMT\r\n< \r\n<http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog>; rel=\"original\",\r\n<http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog>; rel=\"timegate\",\r\n<http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions>; rel=\"self\"; type=\"application/link-format\",",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "codeBlock"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I think we are compliant with the Memento spec as is. ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
           "text": "@Danny Bernstein"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " - thoughts?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
