     "body": "<p>I don't think it's necessary to have an Accept header in the response to a GET on a timemap.  And there's nothing to say we have to advertise 'application/link-format' -  it's just expected that we support it. </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-5\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7089#section-5</a></p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>   GET /timemap/http://a.example.org/ HTTP/1.1\r\n   Host: arxiv.example.net\r\n   Accept: application/link-format;q=1.0\r\n   Connection: close\r\n\r\n                     Figure 27: Request for a TimeMap\r\n\r\n   If the TimeMap requested by the user agent exists, the server's\r\n   response has a \"200 OK\" HTTP status code and the list of Mementos is\r\n   provided in the entity-body of the response.  Such a response is\r\n   shown in Figure 28.\r\n\r\n   HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n   Date: Thu, 21 Jan 2010 00:06:50 GMT\r\n   Server: Apache\r\n   Content-Length: 4883\r\n   Content-Type: application/link-format\r\n   Connection: close\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>We could include a Vary field to indicate that \"Accept\" will function on this resource.  That field exists when one requests a timemap w/o an Accept type.  But it doesn't get returned if you sent in an Accept header, like so:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>\r\ncurl localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -vv -H \"Accept: application/link-format\"\r\n\r\n&lt; HTTP/1.1 200 \r\n&lt; Cache-Control: private\r\n&lt; Expires: Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT\r\n&lt; Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID=E28D3BEA8111021304AD69D52B6E8CD4; Path=/fcrepo5; HttpOnly\r\n&lt; Set-Cookie: rememberMe=deleteMe; Path=/fcrepo5; Max-Age=0; Expires=Wed, 07-Nov-2018 17:11:40 GMT\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#Resource&gt;;rel=\"type\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#Container&gt;;rel=\"type\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#RDFSource&gt;; rel=\"type\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer&gt;;rel=\"type\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog&gt;; rel=\"timegate\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog&gt;; rel=\"original\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions&gt;; rel=\"timemap\"\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://mementoweb.org/ns#TimeMap&gt;; rel=\"type\"\r\n&lt; Accept-External-Content-Handling: copy,redirect,proxy\r\n&lt; Vary-Post: Memento-Datetime\r\n&lt; Accept-Post: text/turtle,text/rdf+n3,text/n3,application/rdf+xml,application/n-triples,application/ld+json\r\n&lt; Allow: POST,HEAD,GET,OPTIONS\r\n&lt; Link: &lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions/fcr:acl&gt;; rel=\"acl\"\r\n&lt; Content-Type: application/link-format\r\n&lt; Content-Length: 236\r\n&lt; Date: Thu, 08 Nov 2018 17:11:40 GMT\r\n&lt; \r\n&lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog&gt;; rel=\"original\",\r\n&lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog&gt;; rel=\"timegate\",\r\n&lt;http://localhost:8080/fcrepo5/rest/super-frog/fcr:versions&gt;; rel=\"self\"; type=\"application/link-format\",\r\n\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>I think we are compliant with the Memento spec as is. <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" data-account-id=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" accountid=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Danny Bernstein</a> - thoughts?</p>",
